<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Shō dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1470–1879</span> · Also known as Second Sho dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Shō dynasty ruled the Ryukyu Kingdom from 1470 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> annexed it in 1879. It was founded by the royal treasurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-en">Kanemaru</a>, who took the throne as Shō En after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-toku">Shō Toku</a>. Under his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-shin">Shō Shin</a> the kingdom reached its height, and from 1609 the dynasty reigned under the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> while continuing to send tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-sho-dynasty.jpg" alt="Second Shō dynasty" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BraneJ · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hidari_mitsudomoe.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
